  <title>Native navigation</title>
  <p>
    Native navigation refers to keyboard input handled by the application rather than Orca.
    Examples include <key>Tab</key>, <keyseq>
      <key>Shift</key>
      <key>Tab</key>
    </keyseq>, <key>Page Up</key>, <key>Page Down</key>, <key>Enter</key>, and <key>Space</key>.
  </p>
  <section id="settings-native-navigation">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Documents</gui> category, <gui>Native navigation</gui> group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Automatic focus mode</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca switches to focus mode when native navigation, such as Tab or Shift+Tab, lands on
          an interactive widget. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Automatic sticky focus mode for web applications</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca detects web applications and web-based desktop apps and stays in focus mode.
          Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Find Options</gui>: Controls what Orca
          speaks while you use an application's Find toolbar.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Speak results during find</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks the line containing each find result. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Only speak changed lines during find</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca speaks a find result only when it is on a different line than the previous
              result. Default: off.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Minimum length of matched text:</gui>
              Sets the minimum number of matching characters required before Orca speaks the
              find result. Default: 4. Range: 0 to 20.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Page load</gui>: Controls what Orca does
          when a document or web page finishes loading.
        </p>
        <list>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Automatically start speaking a page when it is first loaded</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca automatically performs Say All when a document or web page first loads.
              Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
          <item>
            <p>
              <gui>Present summary of a page when it is first loaded</gui>: Controls whether
              Orca presents a summary, such as the number of headings, landmarks, and links,
              when a document or web page first loads. Default: on.
            </p>
          </item>
        </list>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
